      "text": "This guide provides a comprehensive technical blueprint for building a Learning Management System (LMS) prototype using **React, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS**, and **LocalStorage** as your database.\n\n### 1. Project Structure \u0026 Setup\nUsing a feature-based architecture ensures scalability for both user and admin dashboards.\n\n```bash\n# Setup command\nnpm create vite@latest lms-prototype -- --template react-ts\n# Essential dependencies\nnpm install react-router-dom lucide-react clsx tailwind-merge\n```\n\n**Recommended Folder Structure:**\n```text\nsrc/\n├── components/       # Common UI (Button, Input, Card)\n├── context/          # Auth and Global State\n├── db/               # LocalStorage Database Layer\n├── features/\n│   ├── auth/         # Login, Register, ProtectedRoute\n│   ├── courses/      # Lesson player, Progress bars\n│   ├── wallet/       # Referral, Points, Withdrawal\n│   └── admin/        # Management views\n├── hooks/            # useLocalStorage, useAuth\n└── layouts/          # DashboardLayout, AdminLayout\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. LocalStorage \"Database\" Layer\nTo simulate a real database, create a centralized utility that handles CRUD operations and maintains data integrity.\n\n```typescript\n// src/db/schema.ts\nexport interface User {\n  id: string;\n  email: string;\n  role: \u0027user\u0027 | \u0027admin\u0027;\n  points: number;\n  referralCode: string;\n  referredBy?: string;\n}\n\nexport interface Course {\n  id: string;\n  title: string;\n  lessons: { id: string; title: string; content: string }[];\n}\n\n// src/db/localDB.ts\nexport const db \u003d {\n  get: \u003cT\u003e(key: string): T[] \u003d\u003e JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) || \u0027[]\u0027),\n  save: (key: string, data: any) \u003d\u003e localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(data)),\n  \n  // Example: Find user by credentials\n  findUser: (email: string) \u003d\u003e db.get\u003cUser\u003e(\u0027users\u0027).find(u \u003d\u003e u.email \u003d\u003d\u003d email),\n  \n  // Example: Update user progress\n  updateProgress: (userId: string, courseId: string, lessonId: string) \u003d\u003e {\n    const progress \u003d db.get\u003cany\u003e(\u0027progress\u0027);\n    const newProgress \u003d [...progress, { userId, courseId, lessonId, date: new Date() }];\n    db.save(\u0027progress\u0027, newProgress);\n  }\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Core Logic: Referral \u0026 Rewards\nImplement the referral logic during user registration. When a new user provides a code, the \"referrer\" gets points.\n\n```typescript\n// Logic for registration with referral\nconst registerUser \u003d (userData: Partial\u003cUser\u003e, refCode?: string) \u003d\u003e {\n  const users \u003d db.get\u003cUser\u003e(\u0027users\u0027);\n  const newUser: User \u003d {\n    ...userData,\n    id: crypto.randomUUID(),\n    points: 0,\n    referralCode: Math.random().toString(36).substring(7).toUpperCase(),\n  } as User;\n\n  if (refCode) {\n    const referrer \u003d users.find(u \u003d\u003e u.referralCode \u003d\u003d\u003d refCode);\n    if (referrer) {\n      referrer.points +\u003d 500; // Reward referrer\n      newUser.points +\u003d 100;   // Reward new user\n      newUser.referredBy \u003d referrer.id;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  db.save(\u0027users\u0027, [...users, newUser]);\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Wallet \u0026 Withdrawal Prototype\nSimulate a financial ledger. Withdrawals are stored as \"pending\" for the admin to approve.\n\n```typescript\nexport interface Withdrawal {\n  id: string;\n  userId: string;\n  amount: number;\n  status: \u0027pending\u0027 | \u0027completed\u0027 | \u0027rejected\u0027;\n  method: string;\n}\n\n// User Dashboard Action\nconst requestWithdrawal \u003d (amount: number, method: string) \u003d\u003e {\n  const currentUser \u003d auth.user;\n  if (currentUser.points \u003c amount) return alert(\"Insufficient balance\");\n  \n  const withdrawal: Withdrawal \u003d {\n    id: Date.now().toString(),\n    userId: currentUser.id,\n    amount,\n    status: \u0027pending\u0027,\n    method\n  };\n  \n  db.save(\u0027withdrawals\u0027, [...db.get(\u0027withdrawals\u0027), withdrawal]);\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Routing \u0026 Protected Dashboards\nUse **React Router 6** `Outlet` and `Navigate` to separate User and Admin spaces.\n\n```tsx\n// src/App.tsx\n\u003cRoutes\u003e\n  \u003cRoute path\u003d\"/login\" element\u003d{\u003cLogin /\u003e} /\u003e\n  \n  {/* User Dashboard */}\n  \u003cRoute element\u003d{\u003cProtectedRoute role\u003d\"user\" /\u003e}\u003e\n    \u003cRoute path\u003d\"/dashboard\" element\u003d{\u003cDashboardLayout /\u003e}\u003e\n      \u003cRoute index element\u003d{\u003cOverview /\u003e} /\u003e\n      \u003cRoute path\u003d\"courses\" element\u003d{\u003cCourseList /\u003e} /\u003e\n      \u003cRoute path\u003d\"wallet\" element\u003d{\u003cWalletView /\u003e} /\u003e\n    \u003c/Route\u003e\n  \u003c/Route\u003e\n\n  {/* Admin Dashboard */}\n  \u003cRoute element\u003d{\u003cProtectedRoute role\u003d\"admin\" /\u003e}\u003e\n    \u003cRoute path\u003d\"/admin\" element\u003d{\u003cAdminLayout /\u003e}\u003e\n      \u003cRoute path\u003d\"users\" element\u003d{\u003cUserManagement /\u003e} /\u003e\n      \u003cRoute path\u003d\"withdrawals\" element\u003d{\u003cWithdrawalRequests /\u003e} /\u003e\n    \u003c/Route\u003e\n  \u003c/Route\u003e\n\u003c/Routes\u003e\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Responsive UI Components (Tailwind)\n*   **Progress Bar:** Use `w-[${percentage}%]` for lesson tracking.\n*   **Metric Cards:** Use simple grid layouts `grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4` for Wallet/Point totals.\n*   **Lesson Player:** A vertical sidebar for lesson navigation on desktop, shifting to a bottom sheet or hidden drawer on mobile.\n\n### 7. Admin Management Features\nThe Admin Dashboard should prioritize the following CRUD views:\n1.  **User Management:** Table view of all users with \"Manual Credit/Debit\" buttons for points.\n2.  **Withdrawal Queue:** List of \u0027pending\u0027 status requests with **Approve** and **Reject** buttons that update the withdrawal status in the LocalStorage list.\n3.  **Course Builder:** A form to add JSON objects representing new courses/lessons to the `courses` key.",
